{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791140697,"nonce":"yTTtkTOcNW0eI/ZjDdbRL1qddaE=","title":"taffy 0.6 collapses a max-content row to 0 when an item has flex-shrink 0 and a negative margin","message":"Reported by the ashui session (their git-bug 02581ef) and reproduced in\ncrates/blinc_layout/tests/taffy_negative_margin.rs, which is #[ignore]d\npending the decision below.\n\nThree 40px items, all but the first with margin-left -10px and\nflex-shrink 0, in a content-sized row. The row's width comes out 0\ninstead of 100, so the next sibling lays out on top of it.\n\nIn taffy-0.6.3 src/compute/flexbox.rs, determine_container_main_size,\nmax-content branch: content_contribution is 30 and flex_basis is 40, so\ndiff is -10. For diff \u003c 0 the fraction is\ndiff / f32_max(1.0, flex_shrink * inner_flex_basis), which with\nflex_shrink 0 is -10 / max(1, 0) = -10. The contribution is then\nmax(1, flex_shrink) * inner_flex_basis * fraction = 40 * -10 = -400, so\nthe item counts as -360 and the line sums negative and clamps to 0.\ntaffy 0.14 divides by f32_max(1.0, flex_shrink) * inner_flex_basis, the\nsame factor it multiplies back by, giving 30.\n\n\nIt takes the MAX-CONTENT path. The same row measured against definite\navailable space comes out at 100. The reproducer had to be switched to\nAvailableSpace::MaxContent before it failed, so a layout that never asks\nfor max-content is unaffected, which is why this has not shown up in\nBlinc's own UIs.\n\n\n1. Upgrade taffy 0.6 to 0.14. Fixes it at the source and brings\n   everything else, at the cost of a large API jump across blinc_layout.\n2. Patch the one line via a [patch] table or a vendored copy. Smallest\n   diff, and it means carrying a fork of the layout engine.\n3. Leave it. ashui works around it with flex-shrink: 1 on the items, and\n   Blinc is unaffected unless something measures at max-content.\n\nWorth weighing against the earlier choice on c4f8ba2, where route 2 was\nrejected specifically to avoid forking taffy for the baseline work.\nOption 2 here reopens that.","files":null}]}